ll Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb The University of Vienna is internationally renowned for its excellence in teaching and research, and counts more than 7,500 academics from all disciplines. This breadth of expertise offers unique opportunities to address the complex challenges of modern society, to develop comprehensive new approaches, and educate the problem-solvers of tomorrow from a multidisciplinary perspective. At the Centre for Sport Science and University Sports, the University of Vienna invites applications for a Full Professor in Training Science with Biological Focus The position: We are seeking an outstanding researcher with a clearly defined research profile and a proven track record in internationally recognized research. The successful candidate\u2019s research should focus on the scientific foundations and further development of training, exercise performance, performance diagnostics, and competition, as well as their evidence-based application in various areas of sport. A strong commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration with related disciplines in the field of sport and exercise sciences at the Centre, as well as with relevant institutes, faculties, and centres throughout the university, is expected. Experience in collaborating with external, non-university partners and a successful track record in competitive third-party funding acquisition are required. The successful candidate will become part of a dynamic and internationally oriented research environment. As Austria\u2019s largest research institution in the field of sports and human movement science, the Centre offers excellent conditions for innovative and independent research, interdisciplinary collaboration, and active involvement in national and international scientific networks. Your academic profile: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Doctoral degree/PhD \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Outstanding research achievements, excellent publication and funding record, international reputation \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Experience in designing and managing large research projects \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Excellent teaching and supervision skills at the bachelor's, master's, and doctoral level \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Proven leadership qualities \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Gender and diversity competence \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Willingness to take on organisational and administrative responsibilities within the Faculty/Centre and/or the University The University of Vienna expects the successful candidate to acquire, within three years, proficiency in German sufficient for teaching in bachelor\u2019s programmes and for participation in university committees. We offer: a dynamic research environment a wide range of research and teaching support services attractive working conditions in a city with a high quality of life an attractive salary according to the Collective Bargaining Agreement for University Staff (\u00a798 UG, level A1, to be negotiated individually) and an organisational retirement plan a \u201cstart-up package\u201d, in particular for the initiation of research projects comprehensive and personalised support for newly appointed professors and their families throughout their move and transition to Vienna Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Application documents: Please submit a single PDF file (LastName_FirstName.pdf) containing the following information in English via e-mail to the Head of the Centre, Assoc.-Prof. Dr. Barbara Wessner ( barbara.wessner@univie.ac.at ): 1. Letter of motivation 2. Academic curriculum vitae o \u00a0 \u00a0education and training o \u00a0 \u00a0positions held to date o \u00a0 \u00a0career breaks (e.g. parental, family or other care periods) o \u00a0 \u00a0awards and honours o \u00a0 \u00a0commissions of trust o \u00a0 \u00a0previous and current cooperation partners o \u00a0 \u00a0list of most important acquired third-party funding as principal investigator, and, if applicable, of inventions/patents o \u00a0 \u00a0list of most important scientific talks (max. 10) o \u00a0 \u00a0list of courses taught (presented in a clear, concise format) o \u00a0 \u00a0supervision activities (Master and PhD) 3. List of publications and a link to your ORCID record 4. Research statement o \u00a0 \u00a0most important research achievements (max. 2 pages) and planned future research activities (max. 4 pages) o \u00a0 \u00a0synopsis of five key publications with relevance to the position advertised 5. Teaching and supervision statement o \u00a0 \u00a0teaching and supervision concept, with particular reference to teaching and learning methods, diverse student audiences, class sizes and types of courses (max. 2 pages) Appendices to application document: a. Five key publications as electronic full text version b. Teaching evaluations (if available, compiled into a single PDF file) c. Copies of certificates of academic degrees (mandatory, compiled into a single PDF file) The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women\u2019s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Privacy Policy Reference no.: 6280 Application deadline: 12/15/2026 Professorship Vacancies barbara.wessner@univie.ac.at Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Full Professorships, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies \u00d7 Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookie