All Cookies Accept All Cookies"}, "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Full-Professor-in-Religious-Education-and-Catechetics/1443064933/": {"title": "The position:", "description": "Full Professor in Religious Education and Catechetics Job Details | Universit\u00e4t Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser\u2019s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb The University of Vienna is internationally renowned for its excellence in teaching and research, and counts more than 7,500 academics from all disciplines. This breadth of expertise offers unique opportunities to address the complex challenges of modern society, to develop comprehensive new approaches, and educate the problem-solvers of tomorrow from a multidisciplinary perspective. At the Faculty of Catholic Theology and the Centre for Teacher Education, the University of Vienna invites applications for a Full Professor in Religious Education and Catechetics The position: The holder of the position represents religious education and catechetics in research and teaching in their respective breadth and is actively involved in academic self-administration. The position is physically located at the Faculty of Catholic Theology (KTF) and is organisationally allocated 50% to the Centre for Teacher Education. This requires close interdisciplinary and interreligious cooperation (Protestant, Islamic and Orthodox theology/religious education as well as other subject didactics). The questions of religious education are intensively researched both hermeneutically and empirically. Questions of faith communication as well as the addressee-oriented translation of theological findings are part of the profile of the professorship. Proactive cooperation with church and state officials as well as the Private University College of Teacher Education of Christian Churches Vienna/Lower Austria is expected. The academic qualification is proven by a doctorate in Catholic theology and an excellent habilitation or habilitation-equivalent achievements as well as the successful acquisition of third-party funding. Knowledge of the Austrian school system, church educational work and practical school experience are required. Your academic profile: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Doctoral degree/PhD \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Outstanding research achievements, excellent publication and funding record, international reputation \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Experience in designing and managing large research projects \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Excellent teaching and supervision skills at the bachelor's, master's, and doctoral level \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Proven leadership qualities \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Gender and diversity competence \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Willingness to take on organisational and administrative responsibilities within the Faculty/Centre and/or the University The University of Vienna expects the successful candidate to acquire, within three years, proficiency in German sufficient for teaching in bachelor\u2019s programmes and for participation in university committees. We offer: a dynamic research environment a wide range of research and teaching support services attractive working conditions in a city with a high quality of life an attractive salary according to the Collective Bargaining Agreement for University Staff (\u00a798 UG, level A1, to be negotiated individually) and an organisational retirement plan a \u201cstart-up package\u201d, in particular for the initiation of research projects comprehensive and personalised support for newly appointed professors and their families throughout their move and transition to Vienna Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Application documents: Please submit a single PDF file (LastName_FirstName.pdf) containing the following information in English via e-mail to the Dean of the Faculty, Alexander Filipovi\u0107 ( alexander.filipovic@univie.ac.at ) and Faculty Manager, Rudolf Kaisler ( rudolf.kaisler@univie.ac.at ): 1. Letter of motivation 2. Academic curriculum vitae o \u00a0 \u00a0education and training o \u00a0 \u00a0positions held to date o \u00a0 \u00a0career breaks (e.g. parental, family or other care periods) o \u00a0 \u00a0awards and honours o \u00a0 \u00a0commissions of trust o \u00a0 \u00a0previous and current cooperation partners o \u00a0 \u00a0list of most important acquired third-party funding as principal investigator, and, if applicable, of inventions/patents o \u00a0 \u00a0list of most important scientific talks (max. 10) o \u00a0 \u00a0list of courses taught (presented in a clear, concise format) o \u00a0 \u00a0supervision activities (Master and PhD) 3. List of publications and a link to your ORCID record 4. Research statement o \u00a0 \u00a0most important research achievements (max. 2 pages) and planned future research activities (max. 4 pages) o \u00a0 \u00a0synopsis of five key publications with relevance to the position advertised 5. Teaching and supervision statement o \u00a0 \u00a0teaching and supervision concept, with particular reference to teaching and learning methods, diverse student audiences, class sizes and types of courses (max. 2 pages) Appendices to application document: a. Five key publications as electronic full text version b. Teaching evaluations (if available, compiled into a single PDF file) c. Copies of certificates of academic degrees (mandatory, compiled into a single PDF file) The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women\u2019s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Privacy Policy Reference no.: 6277 Application deadline: 12/15/2026 Professorship Vacancies rudolf.kaisler@univie.ac.at Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Full Professorships, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About 