lytics ist ein Webanalysedienst, der von Google angeboten wird und der den Verkehr auf der Website nachverfolgt und meldet. Cookie-Informationen Datenschutzrichtlinie Nutzungsbedingungen Einwilligung f\u00fcr Cookies vom Anbieter AddThis Meine Auswahl best\u00e4tigen Alle Cookies ablehnen Alle Cookies akzeptieren"}, "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Institutskoordinatorin-am-Institut-f%C3%BCr-Politikwissenschaft/1447662933/": {"title": "Institutskoordinator*in am Institut f\u00fcr Politikwissenschaft Stellendetails", "description": "Institutskoordinator*in am Institut f\u00fcr Politikwissenschaft Stellendetails | Universit\u00e4t Wien Wir verwenden Cookies, um Ihnen die bestm\u00f6gliche Erfahrung mit der Website bieten zu k\u00f6nnen. Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen werden im lokalen Speicher Ihres Browsers gespeichert. Dazu geh\u00f6ren Cookies, die f\u00fcr die Website technisch notwendig sind. Dar\u00fcber hinaus k\u00f6nnen Sie frei entscheiden, ob Sie Cookies akzeptieren, und dies jederzeit \u00e4ndern. Bitte beachten Sie, dass Sie Videos auf dieser Website nur dann sehen, wenn Sie\u00a0auf Alle Cookies akzeptieren klicken! Sie k\u00f6nnen auch Cookies zur Verbesserung der Website-Leistung sowie Cookies zum Anzeigen von Inhalten, die auf Ihre Interessen zugeschnitten sind, ablehnen. Wenn Sie nicht alle Cookies akzeptieren, kann dies Auswirkungen auf Ihre Erfahrung auf der Site und die von uns angebotenen Services haben Cookie-Einstellungen \u00e4ndern Alle Cookies ablehnen Alle Cookies akzeptieren Zum Hauptinhalt Sprache (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Profil anlegen / An- & Abmelden Mitarbeiter-Anmeldung Karriere Uni Wien Alle Jobangebote Sprache (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Profil anlegen / An- & Abmelden Mitarbeiter-Anmeldung Karriere Uni Wien Alle Jobangebote Karriere Uni Wien Jobs in Forschung & Lehre Studienbegleitend & Berufsstart Praedoc Postdoc (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists Tenure Track-Professuren Universit\u00e4tsprofessuren Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation Data & Library Services Facility Management Finanz & Controlling HR IT Kommunikation & Marketing Koordination & Management Labor & Technik Research & Teaching Services Alle Jobangebote Sprache (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Profil anlegen / An- & Abmelden Mitarbeiter-Anmeldung Nach Stichwort suchen Suchen Sie nach passenden Jobs mittels Stichwort, das Sie am Ende mit einem Sternchen versehen. Z.B. \"Organ*\" f\u00fcr Organisationsassistent*in oder \"Univ*\" f\u00fcr Universit\u00e4tsassistent*in Erweiterte Filteroptionen Laden... Jobkategorie Alle Voll-/Teilzeit Alle Allgemeines/Wissenschaftliches Personal Alle Einrichtung Alle L\u00f6schen W\u00e4hlen Sie aus, wie oft (in Tagen) Sie eine Benachrichtigung erhalten m\u00f6chten: Benachrichtigung erstellen \u00d7 W\u00e4hlen Sie aus, wie oft (in Tagen) Sie eine Benachrichtigung erhalten m\u00f6chten: Jetzt bewerben \u00bb Institutskoordinator*in am Institut f\u00fcr Politikwissenschaft An der Universit\u00e4t Wien arbeiten rund 11.000 Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten gemeinsam an den gro\u00dfen Fragen der Zukunft. Ca. 3000 davon haben vielf\u00e4ltige administrative Aufgaben und unterst\u00fctzen damit exzellente Forschung und Lehre. Wollen auch Sie mit Ihrer Arbeit etwas Sinnvolles f\u00fcr die Gesellschaft tun und organisieren f\u00fcr Ihr Leben gern? Wir suchen einen*eine Institutskoordinator*in am Institut f\u00fcr Politikwissenschaft 49 Fakult\u00e4t f\u00fcr Sozialwissenschaften Besetzung ab:\u00a001.11.2026\u00a0 | Stundenausma\u00df:\u00a020,00\u00a0 | Einstufung KV:\u00a0\u00a754 VwGr. IIIb Befristung bis:\u00a028.02.2027 Stellen ID: 6244 Wenn Sie f\u00fcr Ihr Leben gern organisieren, den \u00dcberblick behalten und das am liebsten in einem gesellschaftlich relevanten und facettenreichen T\u00e4tigkeitsfeld, dann willkommen im Team des Instituts f\u00fcr Politikwissenschaft! Denn bei uns arbeiten Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten, deren Expertise zur Beantwortung der dr\u00e4ngendsten Fragen der heutigen Zeit beitr\u00e4gt. Ihre Arbeit unterst\u00fctzt diese fundierten Inhalte koordinativ sowie organisatorisch, und zwar an einem Ort, an dem Austausch und Wertsch\u00e4tzung gro\u00dfgeschrieben werden. Bei dieser Stelle handelt es sich um eine Vertretungsstelle. Die Stelle ist f\u00fcr die Dauer und im Ausma\u00df der Stundenreduzierung des*der Stelleninhaber*in im Ausma\u00df von 20 Wochenstunden bis 28.02.2027 zu besetzen. Ab dem 01.03.2027 besteht gegebenenfalls die M\u00f6glichkeit einer befristeten Verl\u00e4ngerung, wobei sich das Stundenausma\u00df ab diesem Zeitpunkt ver\u00e4ndern kann. Ihr pers\u00f6nlicher Wirkungsraum: Als Institutskoordinator*in am Institut f\u00fcr Politikwissenschaft, einer Subeinheit der Fakult\u00e4t f\u00fcr Sozialwissenschaften der Universit\u00e4t Wien, f\u00fchren Sie qualifizierte T\u00e4tigkeiten verantwortlich selbstst\u00e4ndig aus: Sie behalten den \u00dcberblick bei den zentralen administrativen Institutsagenden und koordinieren diese, unterst\u00fctzen die Institutsleitung, implementieren neue Prozesse auf Instituts- und Verwaltungsebene und agieren als zus\u00e4tzliche Schnittstelle bei der Kommunikation mit vorgesetzten Dienststellen. Ihre Aufgabenbereiche umfassen eine spannende Bandbreite sowie eine Vielzahl an diversen M\u00f6glichkeiten, Ihre organisatorischen F\u00e4higkeiten gestaltend einzubringen. Was uns als Team besonders wichtig ist, ist ein freundlicher und respektvoller Umgang miteinander sowie sich gegenseitig R\u00e4ume f\u00fcr die Verwirklichung eigenst\u00e4ndiger und innovativer Ideen zu geben. Das machen Sie konkret: Sie \u00fcbernehmen koordinative und organisatorische Aufgaben im Team der Instituts- und Forschungsverwaltung (z. B. Organisation, Vor- und Nachbereitung von institutszentralen Meetings auf Ebene der Verwaltung und der wissenschaftlichen Mitarbeiter*innen, Koordination der als Pool organisierten Instituts- und Forschungsverwaltung und der Verwaltungsaufgaben) Sie bereiten Informationen auf und setzen Kommunikationsma\u00dfnahmen f\u00fcr institutszentrale Agenden um (z. B. Erstellung/ Aktualisierung von Leitf\u00e4den, Aussendungen, Implementierung eines Intranetbereichs des Instituts) Gemeinsam mit Kolleg*innen planen, leiten und implementieren Sie neue Prozesse auf Instituts- und Verwaltungsebene und leisten somit einen wesentlichen Beitrag bei der Optimierung der Verwaltungsabl\u00e4ufe Sie unterst\u00fctzen bei der Budgetplanung Sie unterst\u00fctzen die Institutsleitung gemeinsam mit Kolleg*innen bei der strategischen Planung und Ausrichtung des Instituts im Rahmen der Institutskoordination (z. B. Aufgaben im Zusammenhang mit Zielvereinbarungen, Personalstrukturplanung, Evaluierungen, Retreats, Erstellung von personalrelevanten Dokumenten) Sie agieren als zus\u00e4tzliche Schnittstelle bei der Kommunikation mit vorgesetzten Dienststellen und Dienstleistungseinrichtungen (z. B. Teilnahme an Vernetzungstreffen) Sie \u00fcbernehmen Vertretungst\u00e4tigkeiten im Team, speziell in der Koordination von Personal-, Budget- und Raumagenden sowie der \u00d6ffentlichkeitsarbeit des Instituts Das geh\u00f6rt zu Ihrer Pers\u00f6nlichkeit: Abgeschlossenes Hochschulstudium oder relevante Berufserfahrung und nachgewiesene Kompetenzen in den Bereichen Koordination, Organisation, Projektmanagement, vorzugsweise im universit\u00e4ren Kontext Erfahrung mit Personal- und Budgetverwaltung Sehr gute kaufm\u00e4nnische Kenntnisse Sehr gute IT-Anwender*innenkenntnisse (Microsoft 365, SAP, TYPO3) Ausgezeichnete m\u00fcndliche und schriftliche Ausdrucksf\u00e4higkeit in Englisch und Deutsch Ausgepr\u00e4gte Kommunikationsf\u00e4higkeit, routiniert in Teamarbeit und Abstimmungsprozessen Ihr besonderer Arbeitsstil: Sie arbeiten gerne eigenverantwortlich und strukturiert, sind serviceorientiert und finden gerne L\u00f6sungen Sie sind ein*e Teamplayer*in und haben eine sehr hohe soziale und kommunikative Kompetenz Sie zeichnen sich durch Flexibilit\u00e4t, rasche Auffassungsgabe und eine proaktive, praxisnahe Arbeitsweise aus Sie sind daran interessiert, sich regelm\u00e4\u00dfig weiterzubilden Das bieten wir Ihnen: Work-Life-Balance : Sie haben flexible Arbeitszeiten und k\u00f6nnen auch remote arbeiten. Inspirierendes Arbeitsklima: Sie sind Teil eines engagierten Teams mit diversem universit\u00e4ren Background, in einer lockeren Arbeitsumgebung. Gute \u00f6ffentliche Anbindung : Ihr neuer Arbeitsplatz ist mit \u00f6ffentlichen Verkehrsmitteln bequem erreichbar. Interne Weiterbildung: Wir bieten Ihnen laufend die M\u00f6glichkeit, Ihre Kompetenzen zu vertiefen. W\u00e4hlen Sie aus einem umfangreichen, kostenfreien Kursangebot. Faires Gehalt: Das Grundgehalt von EUR 3.131,30 (auf Basis Vollzeit) erh\u00f6ht sich, wenn wir Berufserfahrungen anrechnen k\u00f6nnen. Gleiche Chancen f\u00fcr alle: Wir freuen uns \u00fcber jede zus\u00e4tzliche Pers\u00f6nlichkeit im Team! So einfach bewerben Sie sich: Mit Lebenslauf und\u00a0kurzem Motivationsschreiben Abschlusszeugnis Ihrer Qualifikation Dienstzeugnissen \u00dcber unser Jobportal / Jetzt Bewerben-Button Bei inhaltlichen Fragen kontaktieren Sie bitte: admin.politikwissenschaft@univie.ac.at Wir freuen uns \u00fcber neue Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten in unserem Team! Die Universita\u0308t Wien betreibt eine antidiskriminatorische Anstellungspolitik und legt Wert auf Chancengleichheit , Frauenf\u00f6rderung und Diversita\u0308t . Wir streben eine Erh\u00f6hung des Frauenanteils beim wissenschaftlichen und allgemeinen Universit\u00e4tspersonal insbesondere in Leitungsfunktionen an und fordern daher qualifizierte Frauen ausdr\u00fccklich zur Bewerbung auf. Bei gleicher Qualifikation werden Frauen vorrangig aufgenommen. Universit\u00e4t Wien. Raum f\u00fcr Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten. Seit 1365. Datenschutzerkl\u00e4rung Bewerbungsfrist: 23.10.2026 Administration & Organisation Jetzt bewerben \u00bb \u00c4hnliche Stellen suchen: Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies, Administration & Organisation Wird auf einer neuen Registerkarte ge\u00f6ffnet. Wird auf einer neuen Registerkarte ge\u00f6ffnet. Wird auf einer neuen Registerkarte ge\u00f6ffnet. \u00dcber uns Karriere Uni Wien Uni Wien Rechtliche Hinweise Impressum Datenschutzerkl\u00e4rung Barrierefreiheit Manager f\u00fcr Cookie-Einwilligungen Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation Data & Library Services Facility Management Finanz & Controlling HR IT Kommunikation & Marketing Koordination & Management Labor & Technik Research & Teaching Services Jobs in Forschung & Lehre Studienbegleitend & Berufsstart Praedoc Postdoc Tenure Track-Professuren Universit\u00e4tsprofessuren Alle Jobangebote Alle Jobangebote \u00d7 Manager f\u00fcr Cookie-Einwilligungen Wenn Sie eine Website besuchen, kann diese Informationen zu Ihrem Browser - meistens in Form von Cookies - speichern und abrufen. Da wir Ihr Recht auf Privatsph\u00e4re respektieren, k\u00f6nnen Sie bestimmte Cookies ablehnen. Wenn Sie jedoch bestimmte Cookies blockieren, kann sich dies negativ auf Ihre Erfahrung auf der Site und die von uns angebotenen Services auswirken. Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind f\u00fcr die Verwendung dieser Website erforderlich und k\u00f6nnen nicht deaktiviert werden. Notwendige Cookies Mehr Details anzeigen Notwendige Cookies Anbieter Beschreibung Aktiviert SAP as service provider Wir verwenden die folgenden Sitzungs-Cookies, die alle f\u00fcr die Funktionsf\u00e4higkeit der Website erforderlich sind: \"route\" wird f\u00fcr Sitzungs-Stickiness verwendet \"careerSiteCompanyId\" wird verwendet, um die Anforderung an das richtige Rechenzentrum zu senden \"JSESSIONID\" wird w\u00e4hrend der Sitzung auf dem Ger\u00e4t des Besuchers abgelegt, damit der Server den Besucher identifizieren kann \"Load balancer cookie\" (tats\u00e4chlicher Cookie-Name kann abweichen) verhindert, dass ein Besucher von einer Instanz zu einer anderen springt Cookies vom Anbieter SAPasserviceprovider sind notwendig und k\u00f6nnen nicht deaktiviert werden. Funktionale Cookies Diese Cookies sorgen f\u00fcr eine bessere Kundenerfahrung auf dieser Site. So k\u00f6nnen Anmeldedetails gespeichert werden, und die Videoleistung kann optimiert werden. Sie liefern uns Informationen dar\u00fcber, wie unsere Site verwendet wird. Sie k\u00f6nnen diese Cookies jederzeit akzeptieren oder ablehnen. Beachten Sie, dass bestimmte Funktionen, die diese Drittanbieter zu Verf\u00fcgung stellen, beeintr\u00e4chtigt werden k\u00f6nnen, wenn Sie diese Cookies nicht akzeptieren. Einwilligung f\u00fcr alle Funktionale Cookies Mehr Details anzeigen Funktionale Cookies Anbieter Beschreibung Aktiviert Vimeo Vimeo ist eine Serviceplattform zur Bereitstellung und zum Teilen von Videos. Wenn Sie die Vimeo-Cookies ablehnen, k\u00f6nnen Sie keine Vimeo-Videos anschauen und nicht damit interagieren. Cookie-Richtlinie Datenschutzrichtlinie Nutzungsbedingungen Einwilligung f\u00fcr Cookies vom Anbieter Vimeo Werbe-Cookies Mit diesen Cookies werden Anzeigen bereitgestellt, die f\u00fcr Ihre Interessen relevant sind. Sie k\u00f6nnen jederzeit frei w\u00e4hlen, ob Sie diese Cookies akzeptieren oder ablehnen. Beachten Sie, dass bestimmte Funktionen, die diese Drittanbieter zur Verf\u00fcgung stellen, beeintr\u00e4chtigt werden k\u00f6nnen, wenn Sie diese Cookies nicht akzeptieren. Einwilligung f\u00fcr alle Werbe-Cookies Mehr Details anzeigen Werbe-Cookies Anbieter Beschreibung Aktiviert AddThis Google Analytics ist ein Webanalysedienst, der von Google angeboten wird und der den Verkehr auf der Website nachverfolgt und meldet. Cookie-Informationen Datenschutzrichtlinie Nutzungsbedingungen Einwilligung f\u00fcr Cookies vom Anbieter AddThis Meine Auswahl best\u00e4tigen Alle Cookies ablehnen Alle Cookies akzeptieren"}, "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral-Vienna-Network-for-Atmospheric-Research-%28VINAR%29/1447669433/": {"title": "University assistant predoctoral", "description": "University assistant predoctoral - Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) Job Details | Universit\u00e4t Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser\u2019s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb University assistant predoctoral - Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. They represent individuals driven by curiosity and a relentless pursuit of excellence. With us, they find the space to try things out and unfold their potential. Are you inspired by their passion and determination? We are currently seeking a/an University assistant predoctoral - Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) 51 Faculty of Physics Job vacancy starting:\u00a011/01/2026 | Working hours:\u00a0\u00a030.00\u00a0 | Classification CBA:\u00a0\u00a748 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until:\u00a010/31/2030 Job ID: 6233 Are you interested in experimental aerosol physics, in-situ measurements, and both laboratory and field work? If so, join the Aerosol Physics and Environmental Physics (AEP) Group to investigate understudied aerosol components across urban and remote environments. As a pre-doc, you will be part of the AEP Group around Professor Bernadett Weinzierl. The AEP Group combines highly sophisticated laboratory, ground-based and aircraft measurements with innovative modelling to study the fundamental physical and chemical properties of aerosol particles and clouds. Current research covers various areas of aerosol science and spans the whole size spectrum from the nano- to the microscale. We are looking for a motivated pre-doctoral scientist to extend our team. The employment duration is 4 years. Your personal sphere of influence: As a pre-doc university assistant in this 4-year position, you will be part of the Aerosol Physics and Environmental Physics Group around Professor Bernadett Weinzierl. The overall aim of this position is the characterization of the atmospheric aerosol collected at the Aerosols Observatory of the University of Vienna, which is in the process of becoming a National Facility within the pan-European Aerosol, Clouds and Trace Gases Research Infrastructure ACTRIS, and comparison to the aerosol data measured at the Sonnblick Observatory, Austria. Specifically, you will focus on the determination of optical and microphysical properties of atmospheric aerosols measured at these two stations, one representing urban background environment, and the other one, remote atmosphere at 3100 m in altitude. The position is offered within the Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) and involves collaboration with colleagues at GeoSphere Austria and the Department of Meteorology and Geophysics at the Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy, University of Vienna. The employment duration is 4 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a nonextension declaration. Your future tasks: Active participation in research, teaching & administration, which means: You will be involved in unique research projects in which we collaborate with top scientific institutions Your work will focus on rarely-studied aerosol components (including microplastics and others) at urban and remote sites in the framework of ACTRIS and beyond You will set up, characterize, maintain and operate ACTRIS instrumentation such as Aethalometer (AE), Nephelometer, Aerodynamic Particle Sizer (APS) in order to measure the aerosol microphysical and optical properties sampling from a PM10 inlet at the Aerosol Observatory You will characterize instruments in the laboratory, perform aerosol measurements at the Aerosol Observatory, process, analyze and interpret the aerosol data with respect to aerosol microphysical and optical properties You will compare data obtained at the Aerosol Observatory (urban background) in Vienna and the Sonnblick Observatory (remote atmosphere) You will collaborate within VINAR, GeoSphere Austria (Sonnblick Observatory) and the Department of Meteorology and Geophysics at the Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy, University of Vienna (FLEXPART modelling) You will work on your dissertation and towards its completion in time. You will present your research plan to the faculty and complete a dissertation agreement within 12\u201318 months. This will be reviewed and adapted on an annual basis You will actively and continuously perform literature search to independently locate relevant journal articles You will contribute to teaching (lab courses, exercise classes) within the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement You will fill some administrative tasks, contributing to the success and self-organization of the group for research, teaching and administration You will contribute to outreach by publications, conference presentations and public activities This is part of your personality: Compulsory: Master's degree (or equivalent) in physics and/or aerosol-related topics such as atmospheric sciences, aerosol chemistry, meteorology, or similar Affinity for practical work; ideally, you have experience in experimental/technical work An excellent command of written and spoken English (C1 or higher) Experience in programming (e.g., Python) to perform your data analysis Reliable, regular presence in the laboratory on site in Vienna Willingness to travel: measurement campaigns may involve fieldwork away from the office, including national and international stays You are a team player with good social/communication skills, as the goal will only be achieved in a team Class B driving license Desirable: Knowledge in atmospheric and/or aerosol physics and experimental work Experience with common aerosol particle detection and characterization techniques, in particular with measurements of aerosol microphysical and optical properties, is considered an asset Experience in building experimental setups, instrument characterization, and calibration Experience with in-field measurement campaigns is an asset Initiative in finding solutions for technical and scientific problems What we offer: Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Potential for development : Success in life depends on what you make of it, but if you are ambitious and successful, there are plenty of opportunities to connect you to many relevant top research groups in the world. Internal further training & coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from \u2013 free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3,776.10 (full-time basis, 14x p.a.) increases if we can credit professional experience. The duration of employment is 4 years . Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: With your scientific curriculum vitae. A summary of your previous academic and research achievements. A short statement on your research interests for the future. Your Bachelor\u2019s and Master\u2019s degree: an excellent academic degree is a good entrance statement for this position. Note that while a Master\u2019s degree is the usual legal prerequisite for a PhD position at the University of Vienna, we can consider Bachelor\u2019s degrees (preferentially with Honors) in exceptional cases, too. If you have any questions, please contact: Bernadett Weinzierl bernadett.weinzierl@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women\u2019s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection \u200bApplication deadline: 10/24/2026 Prae Doc Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies \u00d7 Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"}, "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1447706033/": {"title": "University assistant predoctoral", "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universit\u00e4t Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser\u2019s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. They represent individuals driven by curiosity and a relentless pursuit of excellence. With us, they find the space to try things out and unfold their potential. Are you inspired by their passion and determination? We are currently seeking a/an University assistant predoctoral 51 Faculty of Physics Job vacancy starting:\u00a012/01/2026 | Working hours:\u00a0\u00a030.00\u00a0 | Classification CBA:\u00a0\u00a748 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until:\u00a011/30/2030 Job ID: 6265 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where more than 7,500 academics thrive on curiosity in continuous exploration and help us better understand our world. Does this sound like you? Then join our accomplished team! The Group Electronic Properties of Materials at the Faculty of Physics at the University of Vienna searches excellent candidates for the subgroup Low Dimensional Quantum Solids. The Group of Electronic Properties of Materials at the Faculty of Physics is a committed team of scientists with the main research focus on low dimensional quantum solids. We dedicate a great part of our research to the growth and spectroscopic analysis of pristine and doped carbon-based molecular structures to unravel their underlying electron transport and optical properties. We aim at understanding which parameters control their unique properties to subsequently engineer them to access their full application potential. Your personal sphere of influence: Your job will be focused on tailoring the electronic and optical properties of 1D and 2D nanostructures via advanced filling reactions and intercalation. Especially, the control of basic correlation effects, doping of interfaces and the concomitant understanding of their influence on charge transfer and hybridization are crucial. The group offers a vibrant and intellectually stimulating research environment where curiosity and scientific excellence thrive. You'll be part of a dynamic, collaborative community of researchers who are passionate about pushing the boundaries of materials science. Our atmosphere balances ambitious research goals with mutual support and collegiality, fostering both independent thinking and teamwork. We offer an active research culture with regular seminars, group discussions and knowledge exchange that keep you connected to the latest developments. We all value open communication, creative problem-solving, and a healthy work-life balance, creating an environment where you can grow both professionally and personally. International collaboration is at the heart of what we do, providing you with opportunities to build a global network while working alongside diverse, talented colleagues who share your enthusiasm for cutting-edge science. You will be associated to the MORE-TEM project and OVID laboratory as well as to the MATE platform. See more information on more-tem.univie.ac.at and ovid.univie.ac.at. Within these projects our group focuses strongly on the development of new techniques combining high spatial, energy & momentum (q)-resolution for nanospectroscopic analysis at all energy scales. This enables us to investigate dispersion and lifetime of primary excitations in nanomaterials such as 2D heterostructures and 1D nanotubes. This facilitates the control of quantum phases, like charge-density waves and superconductivity, to engineer new materials for energy (e.g. batteries, (opto-)electronic devices). Your future tasks: You actively participate in research, teaching & administration, which means: You will present your research plan to the faculty and complete a dissertation agreement within 12-18 months. This will be reviewed and adapted on an annual basis. You will work on and advance your dissertation and towards its completion in time toward successful completion with dedicated mentorship. We expect a large degree of independence paired with a high level of social awareness as the goal will only be achieved in a team. You will contribute to teaching activities (lab courses, exercise classes) both in teams and independently within the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. You will fill some administrative tasks, contributing to the success and self-organization of the group for research, teaching and administration. You will continuously stay informed about the state of the art in your field. You will contribute to outreach by publications, conference presentations and public activities. You will engage with the broader scientific community through conferences and collaborative events. This is part of your personality: You must have a master's degree or diploma in physics, physical chemistry, materials science or a related field. You must have experience either in inelastic electron scattering (EELS), TEM or optical and Raman spectroscopy. You must have basic experience in academic writing. You must have initiative in solving scientific problems. You must have excellent command of written and spoken English. Basic use of German would be useful but is not compulsory. You are a team player. You are motivated to contribute to high-quality teaching and are willing to develop your didactic skills in the course of your employment. What we offer: Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Potential for developmen t : Success in life depends on what you make of it, but if you are ambitious and successful, there are plenty of opportunities to connect you to all relevant top research groups in the world. Internal further training & coaching: The Vienna Doctoral School as well as the department of human resources offer plenty of opportunities to grow your skills in over 600 courses to choose from \u2013 free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3,776.10 (full-time basis, 14x p.a.) increases if we can credit professional experience. The employment duration is 4 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. Occupation group in accordance with collective bargaining agreement: \u00a748 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc). After three years of employment, the salary increases according to the collective bargaining agreement. A PhD project: A project related to cutting-edge research in the fields of materials science and physical properties of new materials. Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible, family-friendly working hours. A city with an outstanding life quality: Vienna has been chosen several times as the most livable city word-wide, with a rich culture, numerous recreational opportunities and beautiful nature surroundings. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is in the center of Vienna and is easily accessible by public transport. Equal opportunities for everyone: We look forward to diverse personalities in the team! It is that easy to apply: With your scientific curriculum vitae / letter of intent With your summary of research interests / ideas for a prospective doctoral project proposal Master's degree / Diploma Via our job portal/ \"Apply now\" button If you have any questions, please contact: Thomas Pichler thomas.pichler@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women\u2019s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection \u200bApplication deadline: 10/24/2026 Prae Doc Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies \u00d7 Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"}, "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-Assistant-postdoctoral-1/1447657533/": {"title": "University Assistant postdoctoral 1", "description": "University Assistant postdoctoral 1 Job Details | Universit\u00e4t Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser\u2019s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb University Assistant postdoctoral 1 The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fueled by curiosity and a deep sense of duty, they contribute invaluable insights to research and teaching, enriching our society. Are you inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? We are currently seeking a/an University Assistant postdoctoral 1 47 Faculty of Psychology Job vacancy starting:\u00a001/01/2027\u00a0| Working hours:\u00a0\u00a040.00\u00a0 | Classification CBA:\u00a0\u00a748 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6279 At the University of Vienna, more than 10,000 people work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700 of them are scientists who, with their curiosity and continuous demand for excellence, conduct top-level international research and teaching. Are you also looking for the right space to develop your potential? We are seeking a/an Your place of work: The Faculty of Psychology at the University of Vienna comprises the Dean's Office, a Student Service Center, four institutes, and the Outpatient Unit for Research, Teaching and Practice. Your future position is based with the new Professorship of Psychotherapy and Psychotherapy Research (Univ.-Prof. Dr. Thomas Probst) at the Institute for Clinical and Health Psychology. The research group investigates Processes and Effectiveness of Psychotherapy and Therapeutic Interventions. Other key research areas of the professorship include: Evidence-Based Psychotherapy Digitalization, e.g., AI, in Psychotherapy The Use of Psychological and Neuroscientific Methods in Psychotherapy Research The working group actively promotes open and reproducible science (e.g., through pre-registration and the sharing of materials and data) and values diverse perspectives. Your future tasks: Active participation in research, teaching & administration, which means: You strengthen the research profile in the field of psychotherapy research. You support research activities aimed at establishing an evidence base for psychotherapy. You plan and conduct your own scientific studies. You publish articles in international peer-reviewed journals. You give presentations at national and international scientific conferences. You participate in science communication activities. You apply for projects and raise third-party funds. You hold courses independently within the scope of the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement . You supervise students. You participate in evaluation measures and in quality assurance. You take on administrative tasks in research and teaching. This is part of your personality: Completed doctoral/PhD studies in psychology or other related fields. Experience in research projects on the evidence base for therapeutic interventions. Psychotherapy training in behavioral therapy, either currently underway or completed. In-depth knowledge of advanced statistical methods (e.g., multilevel modeling). In-depth knowledge of Ecological Momentary Assessment (EMA). Proven research competence and initiative through international publications in peer-reviewed journals. Ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Leadership skills and ability to work in a team. Diligent, independent work methods. Strong sense of responsibility. Excellent written and spoken English and German skills (C1). Desirable qualifications are: Experience with and interest in innovative study designs for establishing the evidence base for therapeutic interventions. Experience collaborating on international, multicenter projects. Work experience with clinical or mentally distressed populations is a plus. Knowledge of psychophysiology is a plus. What we offer: Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours, remote/hybrid upon agreement. Inspiring working atmosphere: You are part of a friendly and supportive team with excellent research infrastructure and connections to other interdisciplinary research initiatives. We will help you refine your research profile and actively support your professional development. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from \u2013 free of charge. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 5.079,50 (14 times a year) increases if we can credit professional experience. We offer an initial contract for three years. This contract can be extended to six years in total by mutual agreement. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: We look forward to receiving your detailed application with a letter of motivation as well as an outline of a planned research project (max. two pages). Please include your academic CV in tabular form (including your list of publications and a list of courses and lectures you have given). PDF attachments of publications, awards/prizes (if applicable). Contact details of of at least two people who could provide reference letters. Degree certificates, official notifications. Via our job portal/ Apply now - button. If you have any questions, please contact: Thomas Probst thomas. probst @univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women\u2019s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection \u200bApplication deadline: 10/24/2026 Post Doc Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: postdoctoral, Postdoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies \u00d7 Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"}, "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Organisationsassistentin/1447540133/": {"title": "Organisationsassistent*in Stellendetails", "description": "Organisationsassistent*in Stellendetails | Universit\u00e4t Wien Wir verwenden Cookies, um Ihnen die bestm\u00f6gliche Erfahrung mit der Website bieten zu k\u00f6nnen. Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen werden im lokalen Speicher Ihres Browsers gespeichert. Dazu geh\u00f6ren Cookies, die f\u00fcr die Website technisch notwendig sind. Dar\u00fcber hinaus k\u00f6nnen Sie frei entscheiden, ob Sie Cookies akzeptieren, und dies jederzeit \u00e4ndern. Bitte beachten Sie, dass Sie Videos auf dieser Website nur dann sehen, wenn Sie\u00a0auf Alle Cookies akzeptieren klicken! Sie k\u00f6nnen auch Cookies zur Verbesserung der Website-Leistung sowie Cookies zum Anzeigen von Inhalten, die auf Ihre Interessen zugeschnitten sind, ablehnen. Wenn Sie nicht alle Cookies akzeptieren, kann dies Auswirkungen auf Ihre Erfahrung auf der Site und die von uns angebotenen Services haben Cookie-Einstellungen \u00e4ndern Alle Cookies ablehnen Alle Cookies akzeptieren Zum Hauptinhalt Sprache (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Profil anlegen / An- & Abmelden Mitarbeiter-Anmeldung Karriere Uni Wien Alle Jobangebote Sprache (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Profil anlegen / An- & Abmelden Mitarbeiter-Anmeldung Karriere Uni Wien Alle Jobangebote Karriere Uni Wien Jobs in Forschung & Lehre Studienbegleitend & Berufsstart Praedoc Postdoc (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists Tenure Track-Professuren Universit\u00e4tsprofessuren Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation Data & Library Services Facility Management Finanz & Controlling HR IT Kommunikation & Marketing Koordination & Management Labor & Technik Research & Teaching Services Alle Jobangebote Sprache (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Profil anlegen / An- & Abmelden Mitarbeiter-Anmeldung Nach Stichwort suchen Suchen Sie nach passenden Jobs mittels Stichwort, das Sie am Ende mit einem Sternchen versehen. Z.B. \"Organ*\" f\u00fcr Organisationsassistent*in oder \"Univ*\" f\u00fcr Universit\u00e4tsassistent*in Erweiterte Filteroptionen Laden... Jobkategorie Alle Voll-/Teilzeit Alle Allgemeines/Wissenschaftliches Personal Alle Einrichtung Alle L\u00f6schen W\u00e4hlen Sie aus, wie oft (in Tagen) Sie eine Benachrichtigung erhalten m\u00f6chten: Benachrichtigung erstellen \u00d7 W\u00e4hlen Sie aus, wie oft (in Tagen) Sie eine Benachrichtigung erhalten m\u00f6chten: Jetzt bewerben \u00bb Organisationsassistent*in An der Universit\u00e4t Wien arbeiten \u00fcber 10.000 Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten gemeinsam an den gro\u00dfen Fragen der Zukunft. Rund 2.900 davon haben vielf\u00e4ltige administrative Aufgaben und unterst\u00fctzen damit exzellente Forschung und Lehre. Wollen auch Sie mit Ihrer Arbeit etwas Sinnvolles f\u00fcr die Gesellschaft tun und organisieren f\u00fcr Ihr Leben gern? Wir suchen eine*n Organisationsassistent*in 52 Fakult\u00e4t f\u00fcr Chemie Besetzung ab:\u00a001.11.2026\u00a0 | Stundenausma\u00df:\u00a010,00\u00a0 | Einstufung KV:\u00a0\u00a754 VwGr. IIIa Befristung bis:\u00a031.10.2029 Stellen ID: 6323 Wenn Sie f\u00fcr Ihr Leben gern organisieren und den \u00dcberblick behalten und das am liebsten in sinnvollen Projekten, dann willkommen im Team! Denn bei uns arbeiten Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten, die mit ihrer Expertise dazu beitragen wollen, dass die gro\u00dfen Fragen von morgen beantwortet werden k\u00f6nnen. Ihr pers\u00f6nlicher Wirkungsraum: Ihr k\u00fcnftiger Platz ist am Institut f\u00fcr Lebensmittelchemie und Toxikologie der Fakult\u00e4t f\u00fcr Chemie. Sie unterst\u00fctzen das zentrale Administrationsteam am Institut und f\u00fchren Verwaltungsaufgaben rund um Social Media, Homepage, Personal, Budget und Lehre eigenst\u00e4ndig durch. Ein Gro\u00dfteil der Kommunikation findet in Englisch statt. Das Arbeitsverh\u00e4ltnis ist derzeit auf 3 Jahre bis 31.10.2029 befristet und kann je nach M\u00f6glichkeit entfristet werden. Das machen Sie konkret: Sie betreuen die Homepage und unterst\u00fctzen bei der \u00d6ffentlichkeitsarbeit/Social Media. Sie unterst\u00fctzen bei der Lehre (sowohl organisatorisch, aber auch mit Moodle) sowie bei der Lehrplanung. Sie bereiten selbst\u00e4ndig Pr\u00fcfungsunterlagen vor (Moodle) und unterst\u00fctzen bei der Pr\u00fcfungsaufsicht und der Auswertung. Sie helfen mit bei der Betreuung von Studierenden. Sie \u00fcbernehmen Funktionen (zum Beispiel Zeit- und Reisebeauftragte*r) in EDV gest\u00fctzten Systemen der universit\u00e4ren Administration. Sie unterst\u00fctzen bei generellen administrativen T\u00e4tigkeiten (Reisemanagement, Organisation von Transporten, Abwicklung von Versicherungen, etc.) Das geh\u00f6rt zu Ihrer Pers\u00f6nlichkeit: Allgemeine oder Berufsbildende mittlere bzw. ho\u0308here Schule (Matura) oder Kaufma\u0308nnischer Lehrabschluss und langj\u00e4hrige Office Erfahrung Berufserfahrung im Office-Management (vorzugsweise im wissenschaftlichen/ universita\u0308ren Kontext) Sehr gute MS Office Kenntnisse (insb. Excel und Power Point) Sehr gutes Deutsch und solide Englischkenntnisse (ab B 2 Level) Erfahrung mit Content Management Systemen (z.B. Typo 3) & Social Media Erfahrung mit SAP ist von Vorteil Ihr besonderer Arbeitsstil: Sie arbeiten gerne eigenverantwortlich und strukturiert, sind serviceorientiert und finden gerne L\u00f6sungen. Sie sind ein*e Teamplayer*in und haben eine hohe soziale und kommunikative Kompetenz. Das bieten wir Ihnen: Work-Life-Balance : Sie haben flexible Arbeitszeiten und k\u00f6nnen auch remote arbeiten, im gegenseitigen Einvernehmen. Inspirierendes Arbeitsklima: Sie sind Teil eines engagierten Teams mit diversem universit\u00e4ren Background, in einer lockeren Arbeitsumgebung. Gute \u00f6ffentliche Anbindung : Ihr neuer Arbeitsplatz ist mit \u00f6ffentlichen Verkehrsmitteln bequem erreichbar. Interne Weiterbildung: Wir bieten Ihnen laufend die M\u00f6glichkeit, Ihre Kompetenzen zu vertiefen.W\u00e4hlen Sie aus einem umfangreichen, kostenfreien Kursangebot. Faires Gehalt: Das Grundgehalt von EUR 2.759,2 (auf Basis Vollzeit) erh\u00f6ht sich, wenn wir Berufserfahrungen anrechnen k\u00f6nnen. Vertrag: Das Arbeitsverh\u00e4ltnis ist derzeit auf 3 Jahre bis 31.10.2029 befristet und kann je nach M\u00f6glichkeit entfristet werden. Gleiche Chancen f\u00fcr alle: Wir freuen uns \u00fcber jede zus\u00e4tzliche Pers\u00f6nlichkeit im Team! So einfach bewerben Sie sich: Mit Lebenslauf Kurzem Motivationsschreiben Abschlusszeugnis Ihrer Qualifikation (z.B. Lehrabschluss, Matura, Studium etc.) \u00dcber unser Jobportal / Jetzt Bewerben-Button Bei inhaltlichen Fragen kontaktieren Sie bitte: Benedikt Warth benedikt.warth@univie.ac.at Wir freuen uns \u00fcber neue Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten in unserem Team! Die Universita\u0308t Wien betreibt eine antidiskriminatorische Anstellungspolitik und legt Wert auf Chancengleichheit, Frauenf\u00f6rderung und Diversita\u0308t . Wir streben eine Erh\u00f6hung des Frauenanteils beim wissenschaftlichen und allgemeinen Universit\u00e4tspersonal insbesondere in Leitungsfunktionen an und fordern daher qualifizierte Frauen ausdr\u00fccklich zur Bewerbung auf. Bei gleicher Qualifikation werden Frauen vorrangig aufgenommen. Universit\u00e4t Wien. Raum f\u00fcr Pers\u00f6nlichkeiten. Seit 1365. Datenschutzerkl\u00e4rung Bewerbungsfrist: 04.11.2026 Administration & Organisation Jetzt bewerben \u00bb \