tle": "Senior Scientist", "description": "Senior Scientist Job Details | Universit\u00e4t Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser\u2019s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert \u00d7 Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now \u00bb Senior Scientist At the University of Vienna, almost 11,000 people work together on the big questions of the future. Approximately 7,700 of them are academic staff members. These are individuals who, with their curiosity and their continuous pursuit of excellence, engage in international cutting-edge research and teaching. With us, you will also find space to unfold your potential. We are looking for a/an ... Senior Scientist 50 Faculty of Life Sciences Job vacancy starting:\u00a010/26/2026 | Working hours:\u00a0\u00a030.00\u00a0 | Classification CBA:\u00a0\u00a748 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until:\u00a003/14/2027 Job ID: 6316 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where over 7,500 brilliant minds have found a unique balance of freedom and support. Join us if you\u2019re passionate about groundbreaking international research and academic excellence. Ready to be part of our team? Let\u2019s shape the future together! Your personal sphere of play: The Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences has a vacancy for a Senior Scientist. The candidate should have extensive knowledge of HPLC in order to effectively lead research and teaching tasks. We are a dedicated and internationally leading team and offer a creative working environment, flexible working hours and an adequate starting salary. This position is a temporary replacement position. The position is initially limitet until 14 March 2027. Your future tasks: Active participation in research, teaching & administration, which means: Providing technical support for research projects at the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences Routine maintenance and coordination of repairs to analytical and preparative HPLC equipment. Planning and carrying out your own research projects in the field of pharmaceutical chemistry. Publishing research results in English-language journals You will independently hold courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective agreement. You will take on administrative tasks in research and teaching Providing technical support for the chromatopraphic separation of drugs (analytical and preparative). You participate in evaluation measures and in quality assurance. You take on administrative tasks in research, teaching and administration. This is part of your personality: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Completed doctoral/PhD studies in pharmacy/chemistry or similar \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Publications in renowned peer-reviewed journals \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent technical and methodological skills in the areas of separation and analysis techniques (including enantiomeric purity analysis) and high-resolution mass spectrometry \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in independently holding courses \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0High level of written and oral communication skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge of university processes and structures \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge of the following is desirable: Experience with common operating systems and software applications for automated measurement and evaluation of HPLC separations \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent knowledge of English (C1) \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Team player and high social/communicative skills \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0 IT skills What we offer: Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours, remote/hybrid and/or part-time work (upon agreement). Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from \u2013 free of charge. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 5.014,30 (14 times a year for senior scientists postdoctoral; full-time), if we can credit professional experience. The position is currently limited until 14 March 2027. Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: With your scientific curriculum vitae / letter of intent With your list of publications With your summary of research interests (max. 1 p.) Doctoral Degree Contact details of persons who could provide reference letters ... Via our\u00a0job portal/ Apply now -\u00a0 button If you have any questions, please contact: Thierry Langer thierry.langer@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women\u2019s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection \u200bApplication deadline: 10/18/2026 (Senior) Lecturer & Researcher Apply now \u00bb Find similar jobs: Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies, (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E), (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies \u00d7 Co